hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22823","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Isa ibn Faid, from a man, from Sad ibn Ubadah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: There is no commander of ten except that he will come to Allah, mighty and majestic, shackled on the Day of Resurrection; nothing will free him except justice. And there is no one who learns the Quran then forgets it except that he will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, leprous."
"22824","Abu Amir narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Amr ibn Shurahbil ibn Said ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Sad ibn Ubadah, that a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Inform us about Friday, what good is in it? He said: In it are five qualities: in it Adam was created, and in it Adam descended, and in it Adam died, and in it is an hour in which no servant asks Allah for anything except that Allah gives it to him, so long as he does not ask for a sin or severance of kinship, and in it the Hour will come; there is no angel brought near, nor heaven, nor earth, nor mountains, nor stone, except that it fears Friday."
"22825","Hashim narrated to us: al-Mubarak informed us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Ubadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by me, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a charity. He said: Give water to drink."
"22826","Hajjaj narrated to us, who said: I heard Shubah narrating from Qatadah, who said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Sad ibn Ubadah, that his mother died, so he said: O Messenger of Allah, my mother has died, shall I give charity on her behalf? He said: Yes. He said: So which charity is best? He said: Giving water to drink. He said: So that is the water supply of the family of Sad in Medina."
"22827","Abu Salamah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abdur-Rahman, from Ismail ibn Amr ibn Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, from his father, that they found in the books, or in the book, of Sad ibn Ubadah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, judged with an oath along with a witness."
"22828","Abu Said, the freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Sad ibn Ubadah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said to him: Stand over the charity of Banu so-and-so, and beware lest you come on the Day of Resurrection with a young camel carrying it on your shoulder, or on your back, which will bellow on the Day of Resurrection. He said: O Messenger of Allah, turn it away from me. So he turned it away from him."
"22829","Yunus narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Shumaylah narrated to us, from a man who referred it to Said as-Sarraf, from Ishaq ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, from his father Sad ibn Ubadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed this tribe of the Ansar is a trial; loving them is faith and hating them is hypocrisy."
"22830","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Isa ibn Faid, from a man, from Sad ibn Ubadah, who said: I heard more than once and not twice, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no commander of ten except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing will free him from that shackle except justice. And there is no man who recited the Quran then forgot it except that he will meet Allah on the day he meets Him leprous."
"24346","Hajjaj narrated to us, who said: I heard Shu'bah narrating from Qatadah, who said: I heard al-Hasan narrating from Sa'd ibn Ubadah, that his mother died, so he said to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: My mother has died, shall I give charity on her behalf, he said: Yes, he said: And which charity is best, he said: Giving water to drink, he said: So that is the water-house of the family of Sa'd in Madinah, Shu'bah said: So I said to Qatadah: Who says: That is the water-house of the family of Sa'd, he said: Al-Hasan."
"24347","Affan narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir Abu Dawud narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, from Sa'd ibn Ubadah, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: My mother has died and upon her is a vow, will it suffice for her if I free on her behalf, he said: Free on behalf of your mother."
"24348","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shumaylah, a man narrated to me, from Sa'id al-Sarraf, or he is Sa'id al-Sarraf, from Ishaq ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This tribe of the Ansar is a trial, loving them is faith and hating them is hypocrisy, Affan said: And he once narrated it to me without doubt, he dictated it to me first correctly."
